---
import Layout from '../layouts/main.astro';
import { Compass, UserCheck, PenTool, GitFork, FolderGit2, HardDrive } from "lucide-react";

const CURRICULUM_REPO = "https://github.com/apprenti-dev/software-engineering-base";
---

<Layout title="Curricula Catalog — apprenti.dev">
	<section class="py-20 md:py-32">
		<div class="container mx-auto px-4">
			<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
				<div class="text-center space-y-4 mb-12">
					<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold">
						The{" "}
						<span class="bg-gradient-to-r from-apprenti-violet to-apprenti-magenta bg-clip-text text-transparent">
							curricula
						</span>{" "}
						catalog
					</h1>
					<p class="text-xl text-muted-foreground max-w-2xl mx-auto">
						apprenti.dev is curriculum-agnostic — a curriculum is just a Git
						repository. Here's what's available today, and how to put it to
						work as an apprentice, a mentor, or a content creator.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Catalog card -->
				<div class="mb-16 rounded-2xl border border-border/50 bg-card/50 backdrop-blur-sm shadow-lg shadow-apprenti-violet/5 p-8">
					<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 mb-3">
						<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Software Engineering apprenticeship</h2>
						<span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-apprenti-violet/30 bg-apprenti-violet/10 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-apprenti-violet-on-dark">
							Reference curriculum
						</span>
					</div>
					<p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
						The first official apprenti.dev path — 54 tasks across 11 terms,
						covering the practice of software engineering from first
						principles through independent work. It's the curriculum every
						fork starts from, and the reference implementation for the
						curriculum format itself.
					</p>
					<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
						<a
							href={CURRICULUM_REPO}
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
							class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-10 px-5 rounded-md bg-primary text-primary-foreground font-medium hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors"
						>
							View on GitHub →
						</a>
						<code class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">apprenti-dev/software-engineering-base</code>
					</div>
				</div>

				<p class="text-center text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-20 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
					More curricula will appear here as mentors and content creators
					author and publish their own — see
					<a href="/docs/creator-publishing-forking" class="text-link hover:underline">Publishing &amp; forking a curriculum</a>
					in the docs. There's no submission process yet; a curriculum exists
					the moment its repository does.
				</p>

				<!-- Opening a curriculum -->
				<div class="mb-20">
					<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mb-3 text-center">Opening a curriculum in the app</h2>
					<p class="text-muted-foreground text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-10">
						Whichever role you're in, apprenti.dev opens a curriculum the same
						way — from <strong class="text-foreground">More</strong> in the
						app:
					</p>
					<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
						<div class="rounded-2xl border border-border/50 bg-card/50 p-6">
							<div class="inline-flex p-2.5 rounded-xl bg-apprenti-cyan/15 mb-4">
								<FolderGit2 class="h-5 w-5 text-apprenti-cyan" />
							</div>
							<h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Clone repository</h3>
							<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
								Paste a GitHub or GitLab HTTPS URL — your fork, or the
								reference curriculum above. Public repositories clone
								without a token; private ones (and pushing your own work)
								need a personal access token with read/write access to
								repository contents, stored only in this device's secure
								storage.
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="rounded-2xl border border-border/50 bg-card/50 p-6">
							<div class="inline-flex p-2.5 rounded-xl bg-apprenti-peach/15 mb-4">
								<HardDrive class="h-5 w-5 text-apprenti-peach" />
							</div>
							<h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Open local repository</h3>
							<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
								Already have a curriculum folder on this device — cloned
								yourself, or handed to you directly? Point the app at it
								and it works fully offline from there, with no remote
								required until you choose to sync.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Forking for your role -->
				<div>
					<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mb-3 text-center">Forking for your role</h2>
					<p class="text-muted-foreground text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-10">
						A curriculum repository is shared; a fork is where your personal
						work lives. The mechanics differ slightly by role.
					</p>
					<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
						<div class="rounded-2xl border border-border/50 bg-card/50 p-6">
							<div class="inline-flex p-2.5 rounded-xl bg-apprenti-violet/15 mb-4">
								<Compass class="h-5 w-5 text-apprenti-violet-on-dark" />
							</div>
							<h3 class="font-semibold mb-3">Apprentices</h3>
							<ol class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed space-y-2 list-decimal pl-4">
								<li>Fork the curriculum repo to your own GitHub or GitLab account (or just download it as a local folder).</li>
								<li>Open your fork in apprenti.dev with <strong class="text-foreground">Clone repository</strong>.</li>
								<li>Your profile, tasks, reflections, and submissions live in your own personal folder inside your fork — never in the upstream repo.</li>
							</ol>
							<a href="/docs/apprentice-getting-started" class="inline-block mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-link hover:underline">Full guide →</a>
						</div>
						<div class="rounded-2xl border border-border/50 bg-card/50 p-6">
							<div class="inline-flex p-2.5 rounded-xl bg-apprenti-magenta/15 mb-4">
								<UserCheck class="h-5 w-5 text-apprenti-magenta" />
							</div>
							<h3 class="font-semibold mb-3">Mentors</h3>
							<ol class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed space-y-2 list-decimal pl-4">
								<li>Fork the curriculum repo — your fork pairs with the apprentice(s) you mentor.</li>
								<li>Give your apprentice access to that fork, then each of you opens it with <strong class="text-foreground">Clone repository</strong>.</li>
								<li>Your reviews live in your own personal folder — the app never overwrites either side's personal data on sync.</li>
							</ol>
							<a href="/docs/mentor-setting-up-repository" class="inline-block mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-link hover:underline">Full guide →</a>
						</div>
						<div class="rounded-2xl border border-border/50 bg-card/50 p-6">
							<div class="inline-flex p-2.5 rounded-xl bg-apprenti-peach/15 mb-4">
								<PenTool class="h-5 w-5 text-apprenti-peach" />
							</div>
							<h3 class="font-semibold mb-3">Content Creators</h3>
							<ol class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed space-y-2 list-decimal pl-4">
								<li>Fork the curriculum repo as a structural reference, or start from an empty repository with a single curriculum manifest file.</li>
								<li>Author tasks and modules by hand (JSON + Markdown) or visually with <strong class="text-foreground">apprenti creator</strong>.</li>
								<li>Push to your own repository — there's no publish button. Sharing a curriculum is just sharing a Git repository.</li>
							</ol>
							<a href="/docs/creator-curriculum-structure" class="inline-block mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-link hover:underline">Full guide →</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- CTA -->
				<div class="text-center mt-20 pt-12 border-t">
					<div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-apprenti-cyan/30 bg-apprenti-cyan/10 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-apprenti-cyan mb-6">
						<GitFork class="h-4 w-4" />
						Free forever — fork anything, anytime
					</div>
					<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Ready to open a curriculum?</h2>
					<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-6 max-w-xl mx-auto">
						Read the full docs for your role, or head straight to the reference
						curriculum on GitHub.
					</p>
					<div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
						<a href="/docs" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-10 px-6 rounded-md bg-primary text-primary-foreground font-medium hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors">
							Read the docs
						</a>
						<a href={CURRICULUM_REPO} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-10 px-6 rounded-md border bg-background hover:bg-accent hover:text-accent-foreground transition-colors">
							View the curriculum repo
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
